SECTION C — TRUE OR FALSE
Write TRUE / FALSE and correct the statement if it is false
31. DECIMAL is generally preferred over floating-point types when exact decimal values are important
TRUE — DECIMAL is suitable when exact decimal precision matters

32. A table can have multiple primary keys
FALSE — A table can have only one primary key constraint, although it may contain multiple columns (composite PK)

33. A foreign key must always be the primary key of the child table
FALSE — A foreign key does not have to be the primary key of the child table

34. A foreign key can reference a key in another table
TRUE — A foreign key references a key in another table

35. DELETE and DROP perform the same operation
FALSE — DELETE removes rows; DROP removes the table definition and data

36. TRUNCATE removes the table structure along with the data
FALSE — TRUNCATE removes rows but retains the table structure

37. VARCHAR and CHAR are identical in how they store character strings
FALSE — CHAR is fixed-length; VARCHAR is variable-length

38. NOT NULL guarantees uniqueness
FALSE — NOT NULL prevents NULL, but does not guarantee uniqueness

39. A CHECK constraint can enforce conditions on column values
TRUE — CHECK can enforce conditions such as salary > 0

40. COMMIT is used to permanently save transaction changes
TRUE — COMMIT saves transaction changes

